OpenStreetMap Nominatim
  When a place is given by name only, the service geocodes it with Nominatim (via geopy).
  Geocoding data (C) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database Licence
  (ODbL): https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright. No OpenStreetMap data is bundled here.

Time zone data
  IANA Time Zone Database (public domain), via the tzdata package. docs/sources/ holds a short
  excerpt of its comments, quoted for reference.
  timezonefinder (MIT licence) is used to infer a time zone from coordinates; its boundary data
  is from timezone-boundary-builder (ODbL), (C) OpenStreetMap contributors.

GeoNames
  No GeoNames data is bundled in this repository. (Place lists used by the LagnaLab website are
  credited on the website.)

Test reference data (tests/engine/golden/)
  Expected values computed with PyJHora (https://github.com/naturalstupid/PyJHora), NASA/JPL
  Horizons (https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/horizons/), and times as printed on prokerala.com and
  drikpanchang.com daily panchanga pages, recorded for comparison only.

Python dependencies (installed from PyPI, not bundled): FastAPI (MIT), Uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause),
Pydantic (MIT), geopy (MIT), timezonefinder (MIT), tzdata (Apache-2.0), PyYAML (MIT).
